<div>LÃ¡adan lacks the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consonant">consonants</a> <span title="Representation in the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)">/p, t, k, É¡, s/</span>. However, it uses <i>b</i>, <i>d</i>, <i>sh</i> (<span title="Representation in the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)">/Êƒ/</span>), <i>m</i>, <i>n</i>, <i>l</i>, <i>r</i>, <i>w</i>, <i>y</i> (<span title="Representation in the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)">/j/</span>), <i>h</i> with the same phonetic value as English. In addition to these, three <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digraph_(orthography)">digraphs</a> require further explanation:</div>
<ul><li><i>th</i> â€“ <span title="Representation in the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)">/Î¸/</span>, a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voiceless_dental_fricative">voiceless dental fricative</a> (always as in English <i>think</i>, never as <i>then</i>),</li>
<li><i>zh</i> â€“ <span title="Representation in the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)">/Ê’/</span>, a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voiced_postalveolar_fricative">voiced postalveolar fricative</a> (as English <i>plea<b>s</b>ure</i>),</li>
<li><i>lh</i> â€“ <span title="Representation in the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)">/É¬/</span>, a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voiceless_alveolar_lateral_fricative">voiceless alveolar lateral fricative</a> (as <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_language">Welsh</a> <i>llan</i>).</li></ul>
<div><b><font size="4">Grammar</font></b></div>
<div>LÃ¡adan is a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verb%E2%80%93subject%E2%80%93object">verbâ€“subjectâ€“object</a> (VSO) language. <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verb">Verbs</a> and <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjective">adjectives</a> are interchangeable. There are no <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Article_(grammar)">articles</a>, and the object is marked by the <i>-th</i> or <i>-eth</i> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suffix">suffix</a>. The <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plural">plural</a> number is shown only by the <i>me-</i> prefix to the verb (<i>wo-</i> is used in some versions of the language). The particle <i>ra</i> following a verb makes it negative.</div>
